###### Article 413-2

Is punished by a term of imprisonment of eleven years to thirty years and a fine of one million (1,000,000) to ten million (10,000,000) CFA francs, anyone who orders the displacement of the civilian population for reasons related to the conflict, except in cases where the security of civilians or military imperatives so require.

###### Article 413-3

The provisions of this chapter apply to offences committed in the context of an armed conflict, that is to say, a conflict which opposes either the armed forces of at least two States (international armed conflict), or in a prolonged manner on the national territory the governmental authorities and organized armed groups or, organized armed groups among themselves (non-international armed conflict). It does not therefore apply to other situations of internal troubles and tensions such as riots, isolated and sporadic acts of violence or acts of a similar nature.

### TITRE II

DU CRIME DE GENOCIDE ET DU CRIME CONTRE L'HUMANITE CHAPITRE 1 : DU CRIME DE GENOCIDE

###### Article 421-1

Constitutes genocide punished by a term of life imprisonment any one of the following acts committed with intent to destroy, in whole or in part, a national, ethnical, racial or religious group or a group determined on the basis of any other arbitrary criterion:
-	murder;
-	serious bodily or mental harm;
-	deliberately inflicting conditions of life calculated to bring about the physical destruction of the group in whole or in part;
-	measures intended to prevent births;
-	forcible transfer of children.

#### CHAPITRE 2 : DU CRIME CONTRE L'HUMANITE

###### Article 422-1

Constitutes a crime against humanity and punished by a term of life imprisonment, the fact for anyone to commit any one of the following acts in execution of a concerted plan as part of a widespread or systematic attack directed against any civilian population:
-	murder;
-	extermination;
-	enslavement;
-	deportation or forcible transfer of population;
-	imprisonment or other severe deprivation of physical liberty in violation of fundamental provisions of international law;
-	torture;
-	rape, sexual slavery, enforced prostitution, forced pregnancy, enforced sterilization or any other form of sexual violence of comparable gravity;
-	persecution of any group or any identifiable collectivity on political, racial, national, ethnic, cultural, religious or gender grounds, or on the basis of other criteria universally recognized as impermissible under international law;
-	enforced disappearances;
-	the crime of apartheid;
-	other inhumane acts of a similar character intentionally causing great suffering or serious injury to physical integrity or to physical or mental health.

###### Article 422-2

The perpetrators of the offences defined in this title also incur the following penalties:
-	confiscation of the proceeds, property and assets derived directly or indirectly from the crime, without prejudice to the rights of third parties in good faith;
-	prohibition from the territory which may not exceed five years.

## LIVRE V : DES CRIMES ET DELITS CONTRE LES PERSONNES

### TITRE I : DES ATTEINTES VOLONTAIRES A L'INTEGRITE PHYSIQUE DE LA PERSONNE

#### CHAPITRE 1 : DE LA TRAITE DES PERSONNES ET DU TRAFIC ILLICITE DE MIGRANTS

##### Section 1 : De la traite des personnes et des pratiques assimilées Article 511-1

For the purposes of this section, trafficking in persons means the recruitment, transportation, harbouring or receipt of persons, by means of the threat or use of force or other forms of coercion, by abduction, fraud, deception, abuse of authority or of a position of vulnerability, or by the giving or receiving of payments or benefits to obtain the consent of a person having control over another person for the purpose of exploitation.
Exploitation includes, in particular, the exploitation of the prostitution of others or other forms of sexual exploitation, forced labour or services, slavery or practices similar to slavery, servitude or the removal of organs.

###### Article 511-2

Constitutes the offence of trafficking in persons: the recruitment, transportation, transfer, harbouring or receipt of a minor for the purpose of exploitation, even if none of the means enumerated in Article 511-1 above is used.

###### Article 511-3

The consent of a victim of trafficking in persons as defined in Article 511-1 above does not eliminate the offence.

###### Article 511-4

Is guilty of trafficking in persons and punished by a term of imprisonment of five years to ten years and a fine of one million (1,000,000) to five million (5,000,000) CFA francs, anyone who commits one of the acts provided for in Articles 511-1 and 511-2 above.

###### Article 511-5

The term of imprisonment is eleven years to twenty-one years and the fine two million (2,000,000) to ten million (10,000,000) CFA francs, when the offence has been committed with one of the following aggravating circumstances:
-	if the victim is a minor of at most fifteen years;
-	if the person is particularly vulnerable by reason of a physical or mental deficiency, or of their state of pregnancy, their advanced age or their state of health;
-	if the act has been committed by fraud or violence, by use of false capacity, false title or falsified or altered documents or false authorization;
-	if the perpetrator makes use of narcotics or any other substance of a nature to alter the will of the victim;
-	if the perpetrator is carrying a visible or concealed weapon;
-	if the perpetrator is an ascendant or a person having authority over the victim;
-	if the victim has been sequestered, deprived of food or exposed in a public or private place of recruitment;
-	if the victim is exposed to dangerous, arduous work or to the worst forms of child labour;
-	if the perpetrator has committed sexual abuse on the victim.

###### Article 511-6

The penalty is life imprisonment when:
-	the victim has died;
-	the victim has suffered mutilation or permanent disability;
-	the trafficking was for the purpose of organ removal.

###### Article 511-7

Is punished by a term of imprisonment of two months to six months,

.

###### Article 511-8

Is punished by a term of imprisonment of three months to one year, any beggar,
:
-	using threats;
-	simulating wounds or infirmities;
-	;
-	entering a dwelling or its outbuildings without authorization of the owner or occupants;
-	gathering, unless it be husband and wife, the infirm person and their guide.

###### Article 511-9

Is punished by a term of imprisonment of one year to three years and a fine of three hundred thousand (300,000) to one million five hundred thousand (1,500,000) CFA francs,

###### Article 511-10

Is punished by a term of imprisonment of six months to two years and a fine of two hundred and fifty thousand (250,000) to three million (3,000,000) CFA francs,
delivers to individuals who incite or employ them to begging.
If it concerns the father and mother, the forfeiture of parental authority provided for by the provisions of the code of persons and the family may be pronounced.

###### Article 511-11

Is punished by a term of imprisonment of three months to three years and a fine of two hundred and fifty thousand (250,000) to three million (3,000,000) CFA francs,

###### Article 511-12

Is punished by a term of imprisonment of six months to two years and a fine of two hundred and fifty thousand (250,000) to three million (3,000,000) CFA francs, anyone who induces a minor to leave the home of their parents, guardian or employer or encourages their delinquency.

