###### Article 611-8

Is punished by a term of imprisonment of eleven years to thirty years and a fine of three million (3,000,000) to ten million (10,000,000) CFA francs, whoever commits a theft with at least three of the following circumstances:
-	if the theft was committed with violence or threats of violence or illegal wearing of uniform or usurpation of an authority function;
-	if the theft was committed at night;
-	if the theft was committed in a group by two or more persons;
-	if the theft was committed by means of scaling, external or internal breaking and entering, underground opening or false keys in a house, an apartment, a room or an inhabited dwelling or used for habitation or their outbuildings;

-	if the perpetrator of the theft secured the use of a motorized vehicle in order to facilitate his enterprise or to favor his escape;
-	if the perpetrator is a domestic servant even when he committed the theft against persons he did not serve, but who were either in his employer's house, or in the one where he accompanied him;
-	if the perpetrator is an employee or apprentice in the house, workshop or store of his employer or if he is an individual working in the dwelling where he stole.

###### Article 611-9

Is punished by a term of imprisonment of twenty years to thirty years and a fine of five million (5,000,000) to ten million (10,000,000) CFA francs, whoever commits a theft on public roads or in vehicles used for the transport of passengers, mail or luggage or within the premises of stations, airports, landing or boarding docks when the theft was committed in the circumstances referred to in the preceding article.
If the victim suffered injuries the penalty is life imprisonment.

###### Article 611-10

Are considered as public roads, the roads, tracks, paths or any other places dedicated to public use located outside built-up areas and where any individual may freely circulate at any hour of the day or night without legal opposition from anyone.

###### Article 611-11

Theft is punished by a term of imprisonment of five years to ten years, and a fine of one million (1,000,000) to three million (3,000,000) CFA francs when it:
-	is committed by several persons acting as perpetrators or accomplices, without constituting an organized gang;
-	is committed by a person holding public authority or charged with a public service mission, in the exercise or on the occasion of the exercise of his functions or his mission;

-	is committed by a person who unduly assumes the capacity of a person holding public authority or charged with a public service mission;
-	is preceded, accompanied or followed by threats of violence or violence against others not having resulted in a total incapacity to work;
-	is committed in a place used or intended for the storage of funds, securities, goods or materials;
-	is committed in a vehicle assigned to public passenger transport or in a place intended for access to a means of public passenger transport;
-	is preceded, accompanied or followed by an act of destruction, degradation or deterioration;
-	is committed by reason of the membership or non-membership, true or supposed, of the victim in an ethnic group, a nation, a race or a particular religion;
-	is committed by a person voluntarily concealing all or part of his face in order not to be identified;
-	is committed in educational or training establishments or, during the entries or exits of pupils or within a time very close to these, in the vicinity of these establishments;
-	is preceded, accompanied or followed by violence against others having resulted in a total incapacity to work for eight days at most;
-	is committed by means of scaling, external or internal breaking and entering, underground opening or false keys in a building even not used for habitation;
-	is committed at night;
-	is committed with illegal wearing of uniform or usurpation of an authority function;

-	is committed during a fire or after an explosion, a collapse, a flood, a disaster, a revolt, a riot or any other disturbance;
-	involved an object that ensured the safety of any means of transport whether public or private.

###### Article 611-12

Theft is punished by a term of imprisonment of five years to seven years and a fine of two hundred and fifty thousand (250,000) to two million (2,000,000) CFA francs when it is committed by an adult with the help of one or more minors aged thirteen to less than eighteen years, acting as perpetrators or accomplices.
The penalties are increased to five years to ten years of imprisonment and a fine of one million (1,000,000) to three million (3,000,000) CFA francs when the adult is helped by one or more minors aged less than thirteen years.

###### Article 611-13

Theft is punished by a term of imprisonment of eleven years to twenty-one years and a fine of one million five hundred thousand (1,500,000) to five million (5,000,000) CFA francs when it involves:
-	a movable object classified or registered pursuant to the provisions of the law relating to the protection of cultural heritage in Burkina Faso, or a private archive document classified pursuant to the provisions of the same law;
-	an archaeological discovery made during excavations or fortuitously;
-	a cultural property that falls within the movable public domain or that is exhibited, preserved or deposited, even temporarily, either in a museum of Burkina Faso, a library, a media library or an archive service, or in a place belonging to a public person or a private person performing a mission of general interest, or in a building assigned to worship.
The term of imprisonment is twenty-one years to thirty years and the fine five million (5,000,000) to ten million (10,000,000) CFA francs when

the offense provided for in this article is committed with one of the circumstances provided for in article 611-7.
The fines mentioned in this article may be raised up to half the value of the stolen property.

###### Article 611-14

Theft is punished by a term of imprisonment of eleven years to twenty-one years and a fine of one million five hundred thousand (1,500,000) to five million (5,000,000) CFA francs:
-	when it is facilitated by the condition of a person whose particular vulnerability, due to his age, an illness, an infirmity, a physical or mental deficiency, is apparent or known to its perpetrator;
-	when it is facilitated by the condition of a person whose particular vulnerability, due to a state of pregnancy, is apparent or known to its perpetrator.

###### Article 611-15

Is punished by a term of imprisonment of six months to three years and a fine of two hundred and fifty thousand (250,000) to six hundred thousand (600,000) CFA francs, whoever counterfeits or alters keys.
The term of imprisonment is four years to ten years and the fine one million (1,000,000) to three million (3,000,000) CFA francs, if the offender is a locksmith by profession.
The court seised orders the confiscation of the false keys and the equipment.
The court may further order on a provisional basis for a period not exceeding five years or on a definitive basis, the closure of the establishment in the cases referred to in paragraph 2.

###### Article 611-16

Is punished by a term of imprisonment of three years to ten years and a fine of one million (1,000,000) to three million (3,000,000) CFA francs, whoever steals from fields animals, beasts of burden or draft, large and small livestock or agricultural instruments.

The same penalties are applicable to the theft of wood in cuttings, of stones in quarries, as well as to the theft of fish in ponds, fish farms or reservoirs.

