###### Article 812-21

In application of Article 902 of the Uniform Act relating to commercial companies and economic interest groups, is punished by a term of imprisonment of three months to three years and a fine of one million (1,000,000) to five million (5,000,000) CFA francs, the liquidator of a company who, knowingly:
-	within one month from his appointment, does not publish in a journal authorized to receive legal notices of the place of the registered office, the act appointing him liquidator and does not file with the trade and movable credit register the decisions pronouncing the dissolution;
-	does not convene the members, at the end of the liquidation, to rule on the final account of the liquidation, on the discharge of his management and the release of his mandate and to note the closure of the liquidation;
-	in the case provided for by Article 219 of the Uniform Act relating to commercial companies and economic interest groups, does not file his final accounts with the registry of the court responsible for commercial matters of the place of the registered office, nor does he request in court the approval thereof.

###### Article 812-22

In application of Article 903 of the Uniform Act relating to commercial companies and economic interest groups, is punished by a term of imprisonment of one year to five years and a fine of one million (1,000,000) to five million (5,000,000) CFA francs, when the liquidation occurs by court decision, the liquidator who, knowingly:
-	within six months of his appointment, does not present a report on the assets and liabilities of the company in liquidation, and on the continuation of liquidation operations, nor does he request the necessary authorizations to complete them;
-	within three months of the close of each financial year, does not prepare the summary financial statements in view of the inventory and a written report in which

he accounts for the liquidation operations during the past financial year;
-	does not allow the members to exercise, during the liquidation period, their right to access company documents under the same conditions as previously;
-	does not convene the members, at least once a year, to report to them on the summary financial statements in case of continuation of the company's operations;
-	does not deposit in an account opened in a bank in the name of the company in liquidation, within fifteen days from the distribution decision, the sums allocated to distributions among the members and creditors;
-	does not deposit, in a consignment account opened in the books of the Treasury, within one year from the closure of the liquidation, the sums allocated to creditors or members and not claimed by them.

###### Article 812-23

In application of Article 904 of the Uniform Act relating to commercial companies and economic interest groups, is punished by a term of imprisonment of one year to five years and a fine of two million (2,000,000) to ten million (10,000,000) CFA francs, the liquidator who, in bad faith:
-	makes use of the assets or credit of the company in liquidation in a manner he knows to be contrary to the interest of the company, for personal purposes or to favor another legal entity in which he has an interest, directly or indirectly;
-	transfers all or part of the assets of the company in liquidation to a person who held in the company the capacity of general partner, limited partner, manager, member of the board of directors, general administrator or auditor, without having obtained the unanimous consent of the members or, failing that, the authorization of the competent court.

###### Paragraphe 8 : Des peines applicables aux infractions en cas d'appel public à l'épargne

###### Article 812-24

In application of Article 905 of the Uniform Act relating to commercial companies and economic interest groups, are punished by a term of imprisonment of three months to three years and a fine of one million (1,000,000) to five million (5,000,000) CFA francs, the presidents, directors or general managers of companies that issue securities offered to the public:
-	without inserting a notice in a journal authorized to receive legal notices, prior to any publicity measure;
-	without the prospectuses and circulars reproducing the statements of the notice provided for in the paragraph above and containing the mention of the insertion of this notice in the journal authorized to receive legal notices with reference to the issue in which it is published;
-	without the posters and announcements in the journals reproducing the same statements or at least, an extract of these statements with reference to said notice, and indications of the issue number of the journal authorized to receive legal notices in which it is published;
-	without the posters, prospectuses and circulars mentioning the signature of the person or representative of the company from which the offer emanates and specifying whether the securities offered are listed or not and, if so, on which stock exchange.
Are punished by the penalties provided for in paragraph 1, persons who serve as intermediaries on the occasion of the transfer of securities, without the requirements set out in this article having been complied with.

##### Section 4

Des peines applicables aux infractions prévues par l'acte uniforme portant organisation des procédures collectives d'apurement du passif

###### Paragraphe 1

Des peines applicables à la banqueroute simple et à la banqueroute frauduleuse

###### Article 812-25

In application of Article 228 of the Uniform Act on the organization of collective proceedings for clearing liabilities, is guilty of simple bankruptcy and punished by a term of imprisonment of three months to three years and a fine of two hundred and fifty thousand (250,000) to one million (1,000,000) CFA francs, any natural person in a state of cessation of payments who:
-	contracts without receiving values in exchange, commitments deemed too large in view of his situation when he contracts them;
-	with the intention of delaying the finding of the cessation of his payments, makes purchases with a view to resale below the market price or, with the same intention, uses ruinous means to obtain funds;
-	without legitimate excuse, does not make to the registry of the competent court, the declaration of his state of cessation of payments within thirty days;
-	keeps incomplete or irregular accounts or does not keep them in accordance with accounting rules and recognized practices of the profession having regard to the size of the business;
-	having been declared twice in a state of cessation of payments within a period of five years, these proceedings are closed for insufficiency of assets.

