###### Article 812-26

In application of Article 229 of the Uniform Act on the Organization of Collective Proceedings for Clearing Debts, any natural person who, in the event of cessation of payments, is guilty of fraudulent bankruptcy and punished by imprisonment of one to five years and a fine of one million (1,000,000) to five million (5,000,000) CFA francs:
-	conceals their accounting records;
-	misappropriates or dissipates all or part of their assets;
-	fraudulently acknowledges being a debtor of sums they do not owe, either in their records, or by published acts or private written commitments, or in their balance sheet;
-	exercises the commercial profession contrary to a prohibition provided for by the Uniform Acts or by law;
-	after cessation of payments, pays a creditor to the detriment of the estate;
-	stipulates with a creditor particular advantages by reason of their vote in the deliberations of the estate, or makes with a creditor a particular agreement from which results for the latter, an advantage at the expense of the debtor's assets from the day of the opening decision.
Any natural person who, on the occasion of a judicial settlement procedure, is punished by the penalties provided for fraudulent bankruptcy:
-	in bad faith, presents or causes to be presented an income statement, a balance sheet, a statement of receivables or debts or an active and passive statement of privileges and securities, that is inaccurate or incomplete;
-	without authorization from the president of the competent court, performs one of the acts prohibited by Article 11 of the Uniform Act organizing collective proceedings for clearing debts.

###### Article 812-27

In application of Article 227 of the Uniform Act on the Organization of Collective Proceedings for Clearing Debts, the penalties provided for in Articles 812-25 and 812-26 above are applicable to partners of commercial companies who have the status of merchants. :

###### Article 812-28

In application of Article 230 of the Uniform Act on the Organization of Collective Proceedings for Clearing Debts, the penalties provided for in Articles 812-29, 812-30 and 812-31 below are applicable to natural persons who are directors of legal persons subject to collective proceedings and to their permanent representatives.

The directors referred to in this article mean all directors in law or in fact and in general, all persons having directly or through an intermediary, administered, managed or liquidated the legal person under the cover or in place of its legal representatives.

###### Article 812-29

In application of Article 231 of the Uniform Act on the Organization of Collective Proceedings for Clearing Debts, the directors referred to in Article 812-28 above who, in that capacity and in bad faith, are punished by imprisonment of one year to five years and a fine of two million (2,000,000) to ten million (10,000,000) CFA francs:

-	consume sums belonging to the legal person by making purely speculative transactions or fictitious transactions;
-	make purchases with a view to resale below market price or use ruinous means to procure funds, with the intention of delaying the finding of cessation of payments of the legal person;
-	pay or cause to be paid a creditor to the detriment of the estate after cessation of payments of the legal person;

-	cause the legal person to contract on behalf of others, without it receiving values in exchange, commitments deemed too significant in view of its situation when these were contracted;
-	keep, cause to be kept or allow to be kept irregular or incomplete the accounting of the legal person under the conditions provided for in Article 228-4 of the Uniform Act on the Organization of Collective Proceedings for Clearing Debts;
-	fail to make at the registry of the competent court, within thirty days, the declaration of the state of cessation of payments of the legal person;
-	misappropriate or conceal, attempt to misappropriate or conceal part of their assets or fraudulently acknowledge being debtors of sums they do not owe, with a view to removing all or part of their patrimony from the pursuit of the legal person in a state of cessation of payments or from those of the partners or creditors of the legal person.

###### Article 812-30

In application of Article 232 of the Uniform Act on the Organization of Collective Proceedings for Clearing Debts, the legal or de facto representatives of legal persons comprising partners indefinitely and jointly liable for the debts thereof who, without legitimate excuse, do not make at the registry of the competent court, the declaration of the state of cessation of payments within thirty days or if this declaration does not include the list of jointly liable partners with the indication of their names and addresses, are guilty of simple bankruptcy and punished by imprisonment of three months to three years and a fine of one million (1,000,000) to five million (5,000,000) CFA francs.

###### Article 812-31

In application of Article 233 of the Uniform Act on the Organization of Collective Proceedings for Clearing Debts, the directors referred to in Article 812-28 who fraudulently are punished by imprisonment of one to five years and a fine of two million (2,000,000) to ten million (10,000,000) CFA francs:
-	conceal the books of the legal person;
-	misappropriate or conceal part of its assets;
-	acknowledge the legal person as debtor of sums it does not owe, either in the records, or by public acts or commitments under private signature, or in the balance sheet;
-	exercise the profession of director contrary to a prohibition provided for by the uniform acts or by law;
-	stipulate with a creditor, in the name of the legal person, particular advantages by reason of their vote in the deliberations of the estate or who conclude with a creditor, a particular agreement from which results for the latter, an advantage at the expense of the assets of the legal person, from the day of the decision declaring the cessation of payments.
The directors referred to in Article 230 of the Uniform Act on the Organization of Collective Proceedings for Clearing Debts, who on the occasion of a preventive settlement procedure are punished by the penalties provided for in paragraph 1:
-	in bad faith, present or cause to be presented an income statement, a balance sheet, a statement of receivables or debts or an active and passive statement of privileges and securities, that is inaccurate or incomplete;
-	without authorization from the president of the competent court, perform one of the acts prohibited by Article 11 of the Uniform Act on the Organization of Collective Proceedings for Clearing Debts.

###### Article 812-32

For the offenses provided for in this section, the court seized may pronounce the prohibition from exercising the profession for a period that may not exceed five years.

