###### Article 812-45

In application of Article 386 of the Uniform Act on the law of cooperative societies, any person who, without being authorized in accordance with the legal and regulatory provisions applicable to this type of grouping, improperly uses the expressions cooperative societies, union of cooperative societies, federation of cooperative societies or confederation of cooperative societies, accompanied by any qualifier, as well as all designations likely to suggest that it is one of the groupings cited in this article, shall be punished by a term of imprisonment of three months to three years and a fine of two hundred and fifty thousand (250,000) to one million (1,000,000) CFA francs.

## BOOK IX: MISCELLANEOUS AND FINAL PROVISIONS

###### Article 900-1

Death sentences pronounced under the previous law are automatically commuted to life imprisonment.

###### Article 900-2

Law No. 043/96/ADP of 13 November 1996 establishing the Penal Code is repealed. The following are also repealed:
-	Articles 736 and 737 of Ordinance 68-7 of 21 February 1968 establishing the Code of Criminal Procedure;
-	Articles 44 to 72, 82 of Law No. 017-99/AN of 29 April 1999 establishing the Drug Code;
-	Articles 1 and 2 of Law No. 007-2004 of 06 April 2004 on the administration of community service work in Burkina Faso;
-	Articles 1 to 5, 13 to 18 of Law No. 26-2008/AN of 08 May 2008 on the repression of acts of vandalism committed during demonstrations on public roads;
-	Articles 1 to 12, 14 to 26 of Law No. 29-2008/AN of 15 May 2008 on combating trafficking in persons and related practices;
-	Articles 1 to 4, 10, 16 to 22 of Law No. 17-2009/AN of 05 May 2009 on the repression of serious banditry;
-	Articles 2 to 12, 14 of Law No. 060-2009/AN of 17 December 2009 on the repression of acts of terrorism in Burkina Faso;
-	Articles 1 to 21 and 23 to 29 of Law No. 11-2014/AN of 17 April 2014 on the repression of the sale of children, child prostitution and child pornography;

-	Articles 87, 116 paragraph 4 and 121 of Law No. 015-2014/AN of 13 May 2014 on the protection of children in conflict with the law or in danger;
-  Articles 1 to 11, 13, 14 to 16, 25 and 40 to 42 of Law No. 022-2014/AN of 27 May 2014 on the prevention and repression of torture and related practices;
-	Articles 3, 42 to 86 of Law No. 04-2015/CNT of 03 March 2015 on the prevention and repression of corruption in Burkina Faso;
-	Articles 5, 8 to 14, 18 and 19 of Law No. 061-2015/CNT of 06 September 2015 on the prevention, repression and reparation of violence against women and girls and the care of victims;
-	Articles 2, 2 bis, 13, 15 to 15 quinquies of Law No. 084-2015/CNT of 17 December 2015 amending Law No. 060-2009/AN of 17 December 2009 on the repression of acts of terrorism in Burkina Faso.
Finally, all previous contrary provisions are repealed.

###### Article 900-3

This law shall be executed as law of the State.

Thus done and deliberated in public session in Ouagadougou, on 31 May 2018
